      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "value": "While I do agree with it Jerome the problem is finding someone who can be considered unbiased in the calls they make when they deal with someone else. I currently am a forum and game moderator for Eternal Crusade and while I have the power to remove people its only done as a last option. I have to gather proof of why I did what I did and document the kick/temp removal as I am not an employee of the company. And this of course is done to protect the company. VRChat can be looked at the same way as they would need to know they can trust the individual they are giving power to. If the Devs are not willing to go that far maybe something like an Most Valuable Chatter status where they can have the Mods/Devs on friends (Not like they dont friend us anyway) but can be on a channel in Discord to report the offender more directly to whoever might be on be it Gunther, VRPill or whoever else might be on at the time. Just a suggestion.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
    {
