      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "value": "An often-cited issue with this is that these \"player mods\" would have to be considered employees of VRChat-- this is not true. Many other games/communities employ a player-populated moderation taskforce in various community settings. A few examples:\n\nGraal Online: Has a \"Graal Police\" volunteer force that has the ability to enforce minor moderation actions on players.\nBlizzard: Has \"VIP\" members on the forums that are given green post text as a distinction, and have closer access to moderators so actions can be taken more quickly.\nSomethingAwful: Almost all moderators are simply forum members that have been entrusted by the administrators with moderating subforums based on their time in the community.\nreddit.com/r/science: A vast majority (about 1000 in total!) of the moderators in r/science are volunteers with limited moderation power.\n\nObviously, this is not a conclusive list. Some of these examples may not be directly relevant, but they do illustrate that such a system can (and does) work.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
    {
      "__v": 0,
      "_id": "59f6c53a32f0b96c6d9ce7ca",
      "author": {
        "_id": "58c6d558ff44e44ada717902",
        "alias": "Rosewood Wombat",
        "aliasID": "65ba012bed6eefce4cea076a",
        "anonymized": false,
        "avatarURL": "https://canny-assets.io/images/26f2f1020fa73f4264e0a3163175003e.png",
        "created": "2017-03-13T17:22:32.352Z",
        "name": "Ron",
        "serviceAccount": false,
        "urlName": null
      },
      "authorID": null,
      "boardID": "58c62efae9868f3662e9d9a1",
      "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
      "created": "2017-10-30T06:22:50.623Z",
      "deleted": false,
      "fileURLs": [],
