  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "This idea came to mind when i saw the recent video that Pewdiepie uploaded, and it reminded me of alot of videos that i saw regarding people who tried out the game for the first time.\nSo my idea is that we have people, chosen by the VRChat Team to act as Helpers/Mods to look out for so-called \"trolls\" and people who are generally misbehaving themselves in public lobby's.\nFor example:\nPerson \"A\" is throwing racials slurs in all directions in a public lobby\nPerson \"B\" initiates a kick to throw out this person\nThe votekick fails\nPerson \"A\" remains in lobby and continues to swear\nSolution: Person \"A\" either Blocks this person, mutes him or calls a Host for help.\nThis usually solves the problem.\nBut what if someone is Hosting an Event and alot of people join who start to \"troll\", ofcourse you could block them all but, that just ain't right.\nAnd you can't just make the world invite-only because then genuine players who are new to the game cannot attend.\nSo i think that someone who has some sort of right to remove the bothersome individuals from the world would be perfect. And ofcourse hosts can do that but they are not Online 24/7.\nSo having people from the Community to come and help out would be the perfect solution to this problem!\n(sry for the long details ;p)\n",
